```python
TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r'E_\{?([A-Za-z0-9^,]+)\}?')
def norm(tok):
    t = tok.strip()
    if t.startswith('E_'): t = t[2:]
    t = t.strip('{}')
    key = t.replace(' ','').replace('\\','')
    mapping = {'C0':'C0','C2':'C2','H2loc':'H2LOC','H2LOC':'H2LOC','C^1,1':'C11','C^{1,1}':'C11','C1,1':'C11'}
    return mapping.get(key, key)
```
Careful with the text `E_{C^1,1}`: regex `E_\{?([A-Za-z0-9^,]+)\}?` on "E_{C^1,1}" matches `E_{C^1,1}` capturing `C^1,1`. Good. On "E_C0" captures "C0".

Chain parse:
```python
def parse_chain(text, path):
    head = text.split('(')[0].split(';')[0]
    parts = re.split(r'\s+(contains|subset of)\s+', head)
    # parts: tok, rel, tok, rel, tok...
    toks = [norm(t) for t in parts[0::2]]
    rels = parts[1::2]
    edges=[]
    for i,rel in enumerate(rels):
        a,b = toks[i], toks[i+1]
        if rel=='contains': edges.append((a,b))  # a > b
        else: edges.append((b,a))               # a subset of b => b > a
    return toks, edges
```
Validate all tokens in known set {C0,C2,C11,H2LOC}; else parse_error.

Rank:
```python
def ranks(tokens, edges):
    # edges (hi, lo)
    import itertools
    order = {t:0 for t in tokens}
    for _ in range(len(tokens)+1):
        for hi,lo in edges:
            order[hi] = max(order[hi], order[lo]+1)
    # cycle check
    for hi,lo in edges:
        if order[hi] <= order[lo]: return None
    return order
```

